---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Prime AI Company fine-tunes open-weight language and image models on customer datasets.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="section-label">About</p>
    <h1 class="heading-display mt-2 text-3xl md:text-4xl">{site.name}</h1>
    <p class="copy-bridge mt-4">Fine-tuning open language and image models on your data.</p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      You bring the domain data. We provide dataset engineering, GPU training, evaluation, and deployment documentation.
    </p>
    <p class="p-instrument mt-4 text-[13px]">
      Each customer's data is used only for that customer's models.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-semibold">Principles</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-muted">
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Delivered to you.</strong> Fine-tuned weights and adapters are delivered under your statement of work, subject to the license of the base model. We never train one customer's data into another customer's models.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Open models.</strong> Where requirements allow, we choose models you can inspect and host yourself over recurring API fees.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Safety built in.</strong> License review, consent for any likeness training, and evaluation gates are part of standard delivery, not optional extras.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="text-text">Your infrastructure.</strong> Training runs on enterprise cloud infrastructure, and can run inside your own AWS account or VPC for regulated workloads.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="copy-caption mt-12">
      New projects: <a href={`mailto:${site.emails.sales}`} class="text-instrument hover:opacity-90">{site.emails.sales}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
